### 错误标注
1. Dayun River → The Grand Canal（大运河标准译名）
2. dilivering → delivering（拼写错误）
3. on the world → in the world（固定搭配）
4. started to be build → started to be built（被动用过去分词）
5. before 2000 years ago → over 2,000 years ago（表达冗余）
6. linked → Connecting（现在分词作状语）
7. river system → water systems（水系固定表达，复数）
8. Huanghe river → the Yellow River；Long river → the Yangtze River（标准译名）
9. it stream → it flows（主谓一致）
10. alongside → through（途经用 through）
11. foods → grain（粮食四级常用 grain，food 表食物不可数）
12. Dayun River develop → The Grand Canal promoted（时态、主谓）
13. business contacts → economic exchanges（经济交流）
14. region → regions（南北两地，复数）
15. continueously → continues（拼写错误，谓语形式）
16. technological knowledge → engineering wisdom（工程智慧）
17. global people → people around the world


### 美化原句
The Grand Canal is the longest artificial canal in the world, whose construction began over 2,000 years ago. Connecting several water systems including the Yellow River and the 
Yangtze River, it flows through many provinces and once undertook the important task of transporting grain and goods. The Grand Canal promoted economic exchanges between the 
north and the south as well as cultural integration. Today, as an important cultural heritage, it is well preserved and continues to display the engineering wisdom of ancient 
China to the world.


### 标准参考译文
The Grand Canal is the longest artificial canal in the world, constructed more than 2,000 years ago. Linking many water systems such as the Yellow River and the Yangtze River,
it runs through a number of provinces and cities and once served as a key route for grain and goods transport. It boosted economic communication and cultural integration between
northern and southern China. Now, as a valuable cultural heritage, the Grand Canal is under good protection and keeps showing the engineering wisdom of ancient China to the 
whole world.
